{"entry_id":"REG-L003_adversarial_audit_and_missing_modality_routing","timestamp_utc":"2026-11-17T15:53:22.934059+00:00","source_id":"5628404318169472","event_type":"lesson_added","tier":null,"status":"recorded","provenance":{"git_commit":"c678696db380cc1995290c47ea90f547bb8d502e"},"details":{"lesson_id":"L003_adversarial_audit_and_missing_modality_routing","finding_id":"F-1111149103659931264-ADV-L003","source_id":"5628404318169472","title":"Prevent synthetic noise leakage, W4 upper-limit leakage, and optimistic Gaia RVS binary clearance","what_happened":"An adversarial audit identified four pipeline weaknesses: (1) generic_outlier injected random Gaussian noise when lightcurves/spectra/vanishing_data were absent, producing phantom open holes and retaining metal-poor halo subdwarf Gaia DR3 1111149103659931264 at Tier C; (2) live sample ingest allowed W4='U' upper limits (w4mpro_error IS NULL) to flood ir_excess flags; (3) _row_to_star_dict compared unpropagated 2016 Gaia vs 2010 WISE coords (0.58 arcsec drift); and (4) Gaia DR3 radial_velocity_error (median uncertainty) was treated as epoch scatter on faint rv_method_used=2 stars without rv_chisq_pvalue.","generic_lesson":"Use deterministic 0.0 for absent modalities in generic_outlier, run metallicity/evolved checks on all generic_outlier stars, require w4mpro_error IS NOT NULL in live excess searches, propagate proper motion before centroid offsets, and convert median RV uncertainty via sqrt(2N/pi) (marking faint unconstrained Gaia RVS stars as binary=not_evaluated).","automated_check":"oddstar.channels.generic_outlier.channel.extract_raw_feature_vector + oddstar.vet.engine.vet_target + oddstar.vet.ir_checks.check_binary","linked_test":"tests/test_lessons.py::test_lesson_l003_missing_modality_routing_and_rv_binary_honesty","added_to_impostors":false,"skill_updated":null,"commit_sha":"c678696db380cc1995290c47ea90f547bb8d502e"}}
